meta {
  name: Get Order Sub-Orders
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/sub-orders
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Fetch the CHILD sub-orders of a COMBINED (diagnostic + radiology) order, each
  fully composed (the same shape as `GET /orders/:id`). `:id` may be the PARENT
  order OR either CHILD — both resolve to the same parent's children, returned
  DIAGNOSTICS first, then RADIOLOGY.

  Background — the combined-order model. When an order is created on
  `/registration/create` with BOTH lab/direct items and radiology items, it is
  stored as a PARENT order plus two CHILD sub-orders:
    • PARENT — carries the patient/referral identity and the main `orderCode`
      (e.g. `ORD-00001`), but NO items/payments/sections. Its billing figures are
      the aggregate of its children, and it is EXCLUDED from the order/billing/
      console lists (`GET /orders` returns only STANDALONE + CHILD rows).
    • CHILD — one per `section` (DIAGNOSTICS / RADIOLOGY). Each carries that
      section's items, its own split payment ledger, its section row, and its own
      suffixed `orderCode` (`ORD-00001-D`, `ORD-00001-R`) = the Sub-Order ID. A
      child is an ordinary order for every other purpose: it appears in its tab,
      can be billed, cancelled, refunded, and have payments received
      independently, and the parent re-aggregates automatically.

  The order-level money (payable, order-level discount, each partial payment) is
  split across the two children proportionally by each section's share of
  `gross − lineDiscount`, with the radiology (last) section absorbing each field's
  rounding remainder so the parts sum back to the whole to the paisa. Example:
  diagnostic 60% / radiology 40% of a ₹1000 partial payment → ₹600 / ₹400.

  Returns `[]` for a STANDALONE (single-section) order. Powers the combined Order
  Overview on `/registration/create`, which renders a separate Test Details +
  Billing block per sub-order. 404 `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if the order is missing,
  soft-deleted, or owned by another tenant.

  Each child element has the full `GET /orders/:id` shape, plus `orderKind`
  (`CHILD`), `section`, `parentOrderId`, and `parentOrder` ({ id, orderCode,
  externalOrderId }) = the Main Order ID the sub-orders are linked to.
}
